  "caveats": [
    "FRONT 1 is scope (a) and stays OPEN: the growing-width cut is a genuine volume law and Addendum 22's theorem does not reach it. But the cut width per nucleon is a FREE PARAMETER -- matching would fix w ~ 2.9, which nothing derives, and at w = 3 the cut is the whole system and the entropy is identically zero. No w is chosen here.",
    "FRONT 2 is scope (b): the invariant is the convexity of the branch decomposition, proved in the corpus (atom-branch-convexity-bound) and not fitted. It excludes reaching AME by any redistribution over the branches of THIS braid word. It does NOT exclude a different word, and says nothing about whether one exists or is derivable.",
    "Front 1 is exact mpmath from the closed form. Front 2's branch traces go through binding_k_solver.per_block_evaluation, which is float64, so the branch control reproduces the committed trace to ~1e-9 rather than exactly. The verdict turns on a 47 % gap, far above that resolution."
